    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Deering's early economy boomed with a lumberyard, printing shop, banks, a hotel, and even an opera house.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ndgenweb.com/mchenry/town-deering.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first church built in Deering was the Congregational Church, marking the town's early religious foundation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ndgenweb.com/mchenry/town-deering.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lutherans later moved an old Free Methodist building to Deering, renaming it the Deering Lutheran Church.",
